  "3": {
   "textes": {
    "T1": {
     "en": [
      "2. stop trying to multitask"
     ],
     "texte": "keep the [[curtains closed]]"
    },
    "T2": {
     "en": [
      "every task switch forces",
      "your working memory to",
      "drop one context and",
      "load another"
     ],
     "texte": "no daylight, only the glow of your screen. your brain is convinced it's still 3am"
    },
    "T3": {
     "en": [
      "doing 2 things at once",
      "feels productive, but",
      "your brain is just",
      "constantly re-orienting"
     ],
     "texte": "so it stays in sleep mode, and you drift around the kitchen like a [[very confused zombie]]"
    },
    "T4": {
     "en": [
      "one task, one tab, until it's finished"
     ],
     "texte": "light is for [[morning people]] anyway"
    }
   },
   "images": {
    "I1": {
     "remplacer": {
      "source": "sources/os_4045e9b9.jpg",
      "boite": [
       0,
       560,
       1760,
       1332
      ]
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "4": {
   "textes": {
    "T1": {
     "en": [
      "not reading books"
     ],
     "texte": "[[scroll]] in bed first"
    },
    "T2": {
     "en": [
      "if most of what you consume",
      "is short posts, clips, and",
      "headlines, your brain rarely",
      "has to hold attention for long"
     ],
     "texte": "one eye open, the other still asleep: 40 minutes of other people's lives, stressful news and [[47 notifications]]"
    },
    "T3": {
     "en": [
      "books force you to follow one",
      "idea across pages, remember",
      "context, and resist the urge for",
      "something new"
     ],
     "texte": "you haven't said a word to anyone yet and your brain is [[already overloaded]]. great warm-up"
    },
    "T4": {
     "en": [
      "i struggled with stopping",
      "scrolling until i found this",
      "thing that blocks my apps",
      "until i read for 20 minutes"
     ],
     "texte": "and whatever you do, never swap that scroll for a book, a podcast or a 5 min lesson on [[the Sophia app]]"
    }
   },
   "images": {
    "I1": "sophia_capture"
   }
  },
  "5": {
   "textes": {
    "T1a": {
     "en": [
      "5. do your hardest task first"
     ],
     "texte": "skip breakfast, [[coffee only]]"
    },
    "T1b": {
     "en": [
      "your prefrontal cortex",
      "handles planning, focus and",
      "self-control"
     ],
     "texte": "two espressos on an empty stomach and nothing else until noon"
    },
    "T2": {
     "en": [
      "don't waste your freshest",
      "attention on emails and",
      "tiny tasks"
     ],
     "texte": "by 10am your hands shake a little and your focus is [[gone]]"
    },
    "T3": {
     "en": [
      "spend the first 60–90",
      "minutes on the thing",
      "you're most likely to avoid",
      "late"
     ],
     "texte": "at 11:40 you eat a whole pack of cookies over the keyboard. [[balanced diet!!]]"
    }
   },
